  "final_decision": {
    "can_be_promoted_with_existing_data": false,
    "reason": "No candidate dataset in the validation tree provides (a) paired single-phone-camera video, (b) ankle dorsi/plantarflexion mocap GT in degrees, AND (c) commercial-permissive license. ASPset has paired video but no foot markers. MPI-INF-3DHP has both but is non-commercial. Fukuchi/ACL/GaitRec are L4 calibration sources (no paired single-phone-camera video). Synthetic subjects do not represent independent biological variance.",
    "recommended_path": "To clear the promotion threshold (lower CCC 95% CI bound >= 0.30) at the current point estimate of CCC=0.644, n_subjects must reach >= 22. Required action: fresh data collection of 13 additional subjects performing the DJ task on a single side-view phone camera with paired marker mocap that includes foot/toe markers (so ankle dorsi/plantarflexion can be derived). Estimated lab time: ~15 min/subject, plus mocap setup.",
    "current_headline_status": "Ankle slot remains 'preliminary additional measurement' in the one-pager. Per-subject CCC point estimate of 0.64 and LoA half-width 9.5deg are inside the Good-tier thresholds, but the lower 95% CI bound at n=9 includes zero (Fisher Z: [-0.034, +0.916]) so the slot cannot carry a 'headline' precision claim."
  }
